<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aimable Pélissier</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1794–1864</span> · Also known as Duke of Malakoff</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aimable Pélissier (1794–1864) was a French general who served for many years in the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>. In 1845 his troops asphyxiated hundreds of members of the Ouled Riah tribe sheltering in caves in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dahra">Dahra</a> by lighting fires at the entrances, an act that caused outrage in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. He later commanded the French army in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimean-war">Crimean War</a>, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sevastopol">Sevastopol</a> in 1855 and was made a marshal and Duke of Malakoff.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aimable-pelissier.jpg" alt="Aimable Pélissier" width="320" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rijksmuseum · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portret_van_maarschalk_Aimable_P%C3%A9lissier_tijdens_de_Krimoorlog_Mar%C3%A9chal_Pelissier_(titel_op_object),_RP-F-F80055_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
